      "content": "If you're concerned about potential ductwork issues, here are some steps you can take to inspect them without tearing down the wall:\n\n1. Look for visible signs of damage or disconnection on the exterior of the house where the ductwork is accessible.\n2. Check for any unusual noises coming from the walls, such as hissing or whistling, which could indicate a leak or disconnection.\n3. Use a flashlight to look for any signs of moisture or mold behind the drywall, which could be a sign of a leak in the ductwork.\n4. If you have access to the attic or crawl space, you can visually inspect the ductwork from above for any obvious signs of damage or disconnection.\n5. Consider using a thermal imaging camera to detect temperature differences in the walls, which could indicate a leak or disconnection in the ductwork.\n\nIf you're unable to identify the issue or if it's beyond your comfort level, it's best to contact a professional HVAC technician to inspect and repair the ductwork. They have the tools and expertise to diagnose and fix the problem without causing significant damage to your property.",
